jobs.description:
Your Next Challenge at Techso



Are you looking to go beyond execution and truly contribute to the technical decisions behind a project?



Techso is looking for a Senior Full Stack .NET Developer to help design and develop digital solutions used by our clients across Canada.



In this role, you'll have the opportunity to work on a variety of projects, contribute to architectural decisions, mentor less experienced developers, and help improve our development practices.



Who We Are



Founded in Montreal in 2014, Techso helps organizations accelerate their digital transformation through three areas of expertise:



IT Infrastructure Management;



Custom Application Development;



Product Lifecycle Management (PLM).



Our team works with recognized clients across a variety of industries, including aerospace, automotive, finance, events, and watchmaking.



At Techso, we value the quality of our projects and relationships over volume. Our core values—Fun, Trust, Efficiency, and Quality—guide both the way we work with our clients and how we collaborate as colleagues.



What You'll Do



**Depending on the projects assigned to you, you will:**  

Design and develop new applications;



Enhance existing solutions by adding new features, resolving issues, and providing ongoing maintenance;



Contribute to the design of innovative solution architectures that meet client needs;



Write and maintain technical and functional specifications;



Estimate the development effort required for new solutions and enhancements;



Participate in production deployments and support change management activities;



Ensure code quality through code reviews, unit testing, and software development best practices;



Contribute to the continuous improvement of Agile practices, continuous integration, and automated deployment processes;



Participate in pre\-sales activities, including effort estimation and technology assessments;



Share your expertise and mentor junior team members;



Stay current with emerging technologies and industry best practices;



Collaborate with multidisciplinary Agile Scrum teams.



The Profile We're Looking For



**You have:**  

A bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field;



At least six years of experience with Microsoft .NET technologies (C\#, ASP.NET, Web API);



Strong experience with front\-end development using React, Angular, or Vue.js;



Excellent knowledge of relational databases, SQL, and tools such as Entity Framework;



A solid understanding of DevOps practices and continuous integration and deployment environments;



Experience working in an Agile and collaborative environment;



Good knowledge of Linux and Windows environments;



The flexibility to travel within the Montreal area to meet client needs;



The ability to communicate professionally in both French and English, as you will collaborate with colleagues and clients located across Quebec and Canada;



Strong interpersonal skills, autonomy, and a collaborative mindset.



Nice to Have



Experience with Azure DevOps;



Knowledge of NoSQL databases;



Experience with ETL processes;



Knowledge of other programming languages such as Java, PHP, Node.js, or Python;



Experience with MAUI, Xamarin, or Telerik;



Experience in solution architecture, mentoring, or technical pre\-sales.



You don't need to master every one of these technologies. Above all, we're looking for an experienced, curious professional who can adapt to a variety of projects.



What Techso Offers



Challenging and diverse projects with recognized clients across Canada.



A flexible hybrid work model adapted to project and client needs.



Bright offices in the heart of Old Montreal, featuring a rooftop terrace.



Complimentary breakfast, snacks, and coffee available at the office.



A vibrant social and sports club, fully sponsored by Techso.



International mobility opportunities through our consultant mobility program.



The opportunity to contribute beyond client projects by participating in internal initiatives that help shape the company's future.



A collaborative community of experts that encourages knowledge sharing and professional development.



Comprehensive private group insurance tailored to your needs.



A culture built on Fun, Trust, Efficiency, and Quality.

Status: Regular Full\-time




In your role as the Retail Technology Solutions Analyst at the North West Company (NWC), you will provide technology support service to all NWC banners to ensure highest service standards – including system/server builds, in\-store data communication diagnostics, and data balancing/recovery activities – all managed remotely. Project activities include Service Request fulfillment as well as participation in major retail store upgrades and/or new store openings.




Joining NWC gives you the opportunity for growth and development throughout the company, an attractive and competitive salary and benefits package, and to be part of a dynamic and diverse culture.




NWC is a leading retailer to under\-served rural communities and urban neighbourhood markets in the following regions: Northern Canada, Western Canada, rural Alaska, the South Pacific islands, and the Caribbean. Our stores offer a broad range of products and services with an emphasis on food. Our value offer is to be the best local shopping choice for everyday household and local lifestyle needs. Check out northwest.ca for more information.




**Your** **Role:*** Provide rotating 24x7 Tier 2 on call support to the store chains to maintain peak operational performance at store level;
* Provide day to day trouble ticket analysis and resolution;
* Consult with Senior Analysts and Manager to determine and deliver solutions for unusual or undocumented problems;
* Deliver preventative maintenance to store systems where necessary;
* Action Service Requests to provision equipment and services;
* On site travel is required to address store system concerns (new store openings, disaster recovery, upgrades, etc.);
* Participate in I.S. project initiatives related to store support/store operations; and,
* Other duties as assigned.

**Desired** **Skills \& Experience:*** Degree or diploma in a computer related program, including Windows based certifications such as MCP or MCSA;
* Minimum 2 years experience providing support in a technical setting;
* Direct experience supporting Point of Sale (POS) applications is needed;
* Knowledge of the SMS/Openfield and Storeline applications is a definite asset;
* Knowledge of systems providing financial service offerings such as prepaid debit cards, account payments, cheque cashing and ATM’s is desirable;
* Ability to travel within Canada to remote locations may be required;
* Strong organizational and time management skills;
* Strong analytical and problem resolution skills;
* Superior verbal and written communication skills; and,
* Ability to manage multiple projects and tasks at once.

**Location:** Gibraltar House, 77 Main Street, Wpg., MB


**Reports to:** Manager, Retail Technology Solutions




We create a collaborative and constructive culture by:




Being Enterprising • Committing to our Customer • Working with Passion • Leading and Developing Others • Demonstrating Respect and Inclusivity • Building Trust




The North West Company is committed to inclusion and diversity and encourages applications from all candidates including but not limited to: all religions and ethnicities, LGBTQ2s\+, BIPOC, and persons with disabilities.




**A competitive salary is being offered along with opportunities to learn, develop and advance throughout the organization. We thank all applicants for their interest; however only those selected for an interview will be contacted.**  



This is an active job opening for a position that is currently available and we are actively seeking to fill  





**For Internal Employees Only:**

Internal employees are required to apply within 5 working days of the position being posted. Applications received after this period may still be considered. This opportunity adheres to the corporate job posting guidelines.

